{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-129453" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129453" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{3}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-4-(-2)=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4+4-2=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=6$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨6,4,-2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129453" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-129453" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129453" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,-4,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,0,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,-4,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,0,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,4,-2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129453" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨6,4,-2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that  $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\ny+2=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-2=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-1$into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-1)+(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}-2+1=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $y=-1$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10195" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-10195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},-1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{2},1,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10195" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-20418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & {x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-20418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(2)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}+2=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(\\frac{5}{2})-(2)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3+2-\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2},2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-20418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-20418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-20418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2},2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},2,-\\frac{3}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2},2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{5}{2},1,\\frac{5}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2},2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-20418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2},2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y-z=3 \\\\  & y-z=2 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(1)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2+1=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(3)-(1)=3\\,⟹\\,x=3+4=7.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=7$,  $y=3$,  and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨7,3,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-10199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨5,2,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨5,3,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨6,2,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,-2,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,3,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10199" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨7,3,1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y-z=2 \\\\  & y-z=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-3=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}+3=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=\\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{7}{2}-3=2\\,⟹\\,x=2-\\frac{7}{2}+3=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{3}{2}$, $y=\\frac{7}{2}$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-129452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+3z=-2 \\\\  & y+4z=0 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+4(3)=0\\,⟹\\,y=-12.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-12$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-12)+3(3)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-2+12-9=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$, $y=-12$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨1,-12,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,-12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨-22,-12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨-22,12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,12,3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-12,3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3+1=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(4)+3(-1)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=8+3=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=11$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨11,4,-1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129569" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-129569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-5,-4,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨11,2,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨11,4,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,-4,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,2,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129569" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨11,4,-1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that  ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation,  we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+3(-1)=-4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-4+3=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(-1)+4(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-3+1+4=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-72978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72978" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & y+3z=2 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-9=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-7)+2(3)=-1\\,⟹\\,x=-1+7-6=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=-7$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,-7,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-129599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-14,-7,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨-14,7,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-7,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,7,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,-11,3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129599" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,-7,3⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+z=-8 \\\\  & y+2z=-1 \\\\  & z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-1-4=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=2$ and $y=-5$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(-5)+(2)=-8\\,⟹\\,x=-8+10-2=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=-5$, and $z=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,-5,2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72972" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-72972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2,-1,-4⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,-4,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-5,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-8,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-3,-3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72972" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,-5,2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7 \\\\  & 2{x}_{3}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-2y+z=8 \\\\  & y-z=-1 \\\\  & z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-0=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=0$ and $y=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x-2(-1)+(0)=8\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{8-2}{2}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3$, $y=-1$, and $z=0.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨3,-1,0⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-10203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,-1,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,1,-8⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-2,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,-1,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10203" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨3,-1,0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+y-z=2 \\\\  & y+3z=6 \\\\  & -z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=6\\,⟹\\,y=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-3$ into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n2x+(-3)-(3)=2\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(2+3+3)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=-3$ and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,-3,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,-3,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,3,-3⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-4,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,4,-3⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,-3,3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,-3,3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=10 \\\\  & y+5z=15 \\\\  & -z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=5\\,⟹\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+5(-5)=15\\,⟹\\,y=15+25=40.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-5$ and $y=40$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(40)-(-5)=10\\,⟹\\,x=10-80-5=-75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-75,y=40$ and $z=-5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-75,40,-5⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-10204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-15,40,-5⟩"] ["math" "⟨-5,-10,5⟩"] ["math" "⟨-75,-10,-5⟩"] ["math" "⟨-75,40,-5⟩"] ["math" "⟨-85,40,-5⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-10204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-75,40,-5⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+z=2 \\\\  & 3y+2z=-1 \\\\  & -z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=2\\,⟹\\,z=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n3y+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}(-1+4)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-2$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,x=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=1$, and $z=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c"} {"question" "q-72981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "q-72981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "93c16086cdff30b528f885c8236d7c9d37bfb874cdc14baef798de686b32bb57"} {"question" "e-4690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+z=2 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4690.json" "file_sha256" "04b85d770b91ec8aecaa9f9591c597fafa61808689376b883f66d7a0a5a3fd04"} {"question" "e-4690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4690.json" "file_sha256" "04b85d770b91ec8aecaa9f9591c597fafa61808689376b883f66d7a0a5a3fd04"} {"question" "e-4691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4691.json" "file_sha256" "6b0ff4079b242844a8429613fc2c1c14900c9b9b4f030f25f29b4a1d588af9a8"} {"question" "e-4691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4691.json" "file_sha256" "6b0ff4079b242844a8429613fc2c1c14900c9b9b4f030f25f29b4a1d588af9a8"} {"question" "e-4692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4692.json" "file_sha256" "1549c393295f8019c940b9e6aa0375aa99f6b9f8d4957cef1bba7ee697973be8"} {"question" "e-4692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4692.json" "file_sha256" "1549c393295f8019c940b9e6aa0375aa99f6b9f8d4957cef1bba7ee697973be8"}] "usage" {"e-4691" [] "q-10204" [] "q-20418" [] "e-4690" [] "e-4692" []} "basis" 1399 "retractions" [[17592186097096 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${x_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3} = 3; x_{2} - x_{3} = \\frac{1}{2}; x_{3} = 2$"] [17592186096843 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n${x + 2y - z = 10; y + 5z = 15; - z = 5$"] [17592186096379 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n$x + y + z = 3; y + z = 2; z = 2$"] [17592186096379 :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that $z=2$. Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad y = 2-2 = 0\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x = 3-2 = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1$, $y=0$, and $z = 2$. Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle$."] [17592186096380 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186096380 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$. We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\nx_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3} = 1; x_{2} + x_{3} =-2; x_{3} = 5\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5$. Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2=-2-5=-7\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13$, $x_2=-7$, and $x_3 = 5$. Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle$."] [17592186096381 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186096381 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1$, $x_2$, and $x_3$. We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n2x_{1} + x_{2} - x_{3} = 0; x_{2} + x_{3} =-2; 3x_{3} = 3\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_3=1\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_2=-2-1=-3\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2$, $x_2=-3$, and $x_3 = 1$. Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186093466 17592186093467 17592186093468 17592186093469 17592186093470 17592186094983 17592186094984 17592186094985 17592186094986 17592186094987] "immutable_fields" [[17592186093465 :answer-field/correct] [17592186093465 :answer-field/id] [17592186093465 :answer-field/key] [17592186093465 :answer-field/type] [17592186094982 :answer-field/correct] [17592186094982 :answer-field/id] [17592186094982 :answer-field/key] [17592186094982 :a